        "point": "Mehlig ranked dynamical mean-field theory first, emphasizing its broad adoption and decades of demonstrated value for understanding correlated electrons.",
        "response": "I agree that DMFT is mature and has reshaped condensed-matter theory. My reservation is that it is a collaborative methodological framework whose boundaries are less sharply defined than a specific predicted and experimentally realized physical effect. That makes the topological-insulator case more readily expressed as a concise discovery citation."
      },
